      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider the choices available for each category: entrees, drinks, and desserts. We will calculate the number of choices for each category and then use the multiplication principle of counting.\n\n1. **Entrees**: There are 4 different entrees available.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of entrees} = 4\n   \\]\n\n2. **Drinks**: There are 3 different drinks available.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of drinks} = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Desserts**: There are 2 different desserts available.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of desserts} = 2\n   \\]\n\nUsing the multiplication principle of counting, the total number of distinct possible meals is the product of the number of choices in each category:\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of meals} = (\\text{Number of entrees}) \\times (\\text{Number of drinks}) \\times (\\text{Number of desserts})\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of meals} = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[\n4 \\times 3 = 12\n\\]\n\\[\n12 \\times 2 = 24\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{24}\n\\]",
