      "text": "To determine the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider each item she can choose from the table and calculate the total number of combinations.\n\n1. **Entrees**: There are 4 entrees available.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of entrees} = 4\n   \\]\n\n2. **Drinks**: There are 3 available drinks.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of drinks} = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Desserts**: There are 2 available desserts.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of desserts} = 2\n   \\]\n\nTo find the total number of distinct possible meals, we multiply the number of choices for each category:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of meals} = (\\text{Number of entrees}) \\times (\\text{Number of drinks}) \\times (\\text{Number of desserts})\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values we have:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of meals} = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nCalculating step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 3 = 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 2 = 24\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24}\n\\]",
